From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] J604 local build: refresh a glassy bar's blur rule on update

omarchy-bar sync_glass() copies default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua into
~/.local/state/omarchy/toggles/hypr only when the copy is missing, so a
changed rule in omarchy-settings never reaches a bar that is already
glassy. omarchy-settings 4.5.0-3.4 adds xray to that rule (the omarchy-bar
layer is full screen; without xray its live blur holds a 120 Hz J604 panel
at 59 fps).

This migration runs once per user through omarchy-migrate (omarchy update
runs it after the packages). On a glassy bar it removes a copy that is
byte for byte the rule Omarchy shipped up to 4.5.0 and runs
`omarchy-bar sync-glass`, which writes the packaged rule and reloads
Hyprland. A hand-edited copy, a copy that is already current, and an
opaque or clear bar are left alone; on those it does nothing.

Upstream direction: omacom/omarchy PR 17849 (c819b32e19, not merged)
makes sync_glass() itself replace a copy that differs from the package;
1792376022 is the merged precedent for a migration that re-runs a glass
sync for the mode in use.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>

---
 migrations/1794094200.sh | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 migrations/1794094200.sh

diff --git a/migrations/1794094200.sh b/migrations/1794094200.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..91d19b51ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/migrations/1794094200.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+echo "Refresh the Glassy bar's blur rule from the packaged toggle"
+
+# The Glassy bar's blur rule is a copy that omarchy-bar writes only when it is
+# missing, so a changed rule in the package never reaches a bar that is already
+# glassy. On a glassy bar, drop a copy that is byte for byte the one Omarchy
+# shipped before and let omarchy-bar sync it again: it writes the current rule
+# and reloads Hyprland. A copy edited by hand, and every other bar background,
+# are left alone.
+[[ $(omarchy-bar background 2>/dev/null) == "glassy" ]] || exit 0
+
+toggle="${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/omarchy/toggles/hypr/bar-glassy.lua"
+source="$OMARCHY_PATH/default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua"
+[[ -f $source ]] || exit 0
+
+if [[ -f $toggle ]] && ! cmp -s "$source" "$toggle"; then
+  case $(sha256sum "$toggle" | cut -d' ' -f1) in
+    # The rule as shipped from the Glassy bar's start up to 4.5.0.
+    033a5926a32c2992d18b4d2cca393119abe1a0cca67266383167af27f5bf9e6b) rm -f "$toggle" ;;
+    *) exit 0 ;;
+  esac
+fi
+
+omarchy-bar sync-glass
